mode: "100644"
text: "# Brief patterns, decision tables & worked examples\n\n## The brief pattern (specificity beats vibes)\n\"[Genre 1-2]. Mood: [one anchor — e.g. 'quietly confident']. Instruments: [2-4 named — 'warm upright piano,\nbrushed drums, soft upright bass']. Vocals: [spec — 'female alto, breathy, conversational' | 'instrumental'].\nTempo: [~BPM or feel].\" Then structure via meta-tags in the lyrics field. Exclude-styles for the leaks.\n\n## The use-case router\n| Job | Move | Rights note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Video background / series theme | Instrumental brief + Extend to length | paid tier; replaces CapCut library-music trap |\n| Podcast intro/outro | 15-30s structured sting ([Intro] heavy) | paid tier; archive the WAV + stems |\n| Ad / client work | Human-in-the-loop version (lyrics/re-recorded part) | strengthens claim; no indemnification — generic styles |\n| Brand sonic identity | Persona → own Voice → Custom Model (owned tracks) | test post-update consistency first |\n| Streaming release | Curate + humanize + DDEX AI flag; no PRO registration for pure-AI | honest performance expectations |\n| Trend-riding TikTok/Reel | NOT Suno — native trending audio in-app | trend reach is native-only |\n\n## The archive checklist (do this now — model deprecation is scheduled)\nWAV downloads of keepers ✓ · stems exported (Auto Split) ✓ · MIDI exported for anything you may re-record ✓ ·\nCustom Model source tracks backed up ✓ · winning style prompts + personas documented ✓.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the rights catch)\n\"made 30 tracks on the free tier before reading the terms. all 30 are non-commercial forever — upgrading\ndoesn't fix them. regenerated the 4 keepers on pro (took an hour), archived wavs + stems same day because the\nold models are getting sunset. also stopped prompting 'like [artist]' — there's an active lawsuit about exactly\nthat, and my ad budget doesn't include a legal defense fund. generic mood words work fine.\" — no-retroactive\ntrap, archive discipline, litigation-aware prompting.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the series theme)\n\"We wanted our videos to *sound* like us — calm, a little warm, never salesy. One brief did it: 'soft jazz,\nquietly reassuring, warm upright piano and brushed drums, instrumental, ~85 BPM.' Generated six, kept one,\nextended it into 15s, 30s and 60s cuts, and now every video opens the same gentle way. One small step: write\none sentence describing how your brand should sound — then make the machine match it, not the other way\naround.\" — brief-first, curation, one theme reused.\n\n## Never\nGenerate anything commercial on the free tier · assume upgrading fixes old tracks · treat commercial rights as\ncopyright ownership · expect indemnification · clone a real artist's voice or fake a collab · prompt artist\nnames for commercial work while litigation is live · skip the DDEX AI flag at distribution · register pure-AI\nworks with PROs · leave keepers unarchived with deprecation scheduled · claim WoopSocial generates or attaches\naudio.\n"
